{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Or it was known.</b> If the ox was a habitual gorer [muad], he pays full damages. Scripture treats the matter of the ox until it reaches <b>If a man steals an ox or a sheep,</b> and all this is because of the slave, who is sold for his theft, for thus it began: <i>When you acquire a Hebrew slave.</i>"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:13.863214737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}